# README — Source Data: Discovery vs. Validation 4-Quadrant Plots In Flowcytometry (Immunophenotyping) Data

## Overview
This file contains the regression results underlying the discovery-vs-validation
scatter ("4-quadrant") plots comparing immune cell population effect sizes across
the three pairwise endotype comparisons (All Low vs Mixed, Mixed vs All High, All
Low vs All High), for both Absolute cell counts and Percentages, in the 2000HIV
cohort (NCT03994835).

## Sheets
Six sheets are included, one per panel of the figure:

| Sheet name | Figure panel | Comparison | Measurement type |
|---|---|---|---|
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_ABS | a | All Low vs Mixed | Absolute counts |
| AllLow_vs_Mixed_PCT | a | All Low vs Mixed | Percentages |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_ABS | b | Mixed vs All High | Absolute counts |
| Mixed_vs_AllHigh_PCT | b | Mixed vs All High | Percentages |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_ABS | c | All Low vs All High | Absolute counts |
| AllLow_vs_AllHigh_PCT | c | All Low vs All High | Percentages |

## Column definitions
Each sheet has one row per immune cell population (restricted to the populations
selected for display in the figure).

- **Cell_Population:** name of the immune cell population/subset (as labeled in
  the figure where applicable).
- **Beta_Discovery:** regression coefficient (β) from the Discovery cohort model.
  This is the x-axis value in the plot.
- **Pvalue_Discovery:** raw p-value from the Discovery cohort model.
- **FDR_Discovery:** Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value from the Discovery
  cohort model. Used (at FDR<0.05) to define "Significant in discovery."
- **Beta_Validation:** regression coefficient (β) from the Validation cohort
  model. This is the y-axis value in the plot.
- **Pvalue_Validation:** raw p-value from the Validation cohort model. Used
  (at P<0.05) to define "Significant in validation."
- **FDR_Validation** (where available): Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value
  from the Validation cohort model.
- **Significance_Category:** the significance/color category assigned to each
  point in the plot, one of:
  - "Validated direction and significance" — FDR<0.05 in Discovery AND P<0.05 in
    Validation, with concordant effect direction in both cohorts
  - "Significant in discovery (FDR<0.05)" — FDR<0.05 in Discovery only
  - "Significant in validation (P-value<0.05)" — P<0.05 in Validation only
  - "Other" — none of the above

## Data processing
- Each population's Beta and p-value were obtained from a separate linear
  regression model of the (inverse-normal-rank-transformed) cell population
  value against endotype group, adjusted for Age, Sex, Season of Collection,
  Genetic PC1, COVID vaccination status, and Time to Laboratory Processing.
- Discovery and Validation cohort models were run independently, then joined by
  cell population.
- Significance classification uses FDR-corrected p-values in the Discovery
  cohort and raw (nominal) p-values in the Validation cohort, consistent with
  the two-stage discovery/validation design.
- Only cell populations included in the pre-specified selected population list
  for each panel are included in these sheets; this matches exactly the points
  shown (labeled or unlabeled) in the corresponding figure panel.

## Relationship to other source data
Sample-level cluster/endotype assignments used to define the comparison groups
are provided in the Endotype_Label sheet of the multi-omics heatmap source data
file. Flow cytometry raw data are deposited in the Radboud Data Repository (RDR)
collection ru.rumc.2000hiv_t0000321a_dsc_002; see the manuscript's Data
Availability statement for access instructions.

